trackers_help_=Trackers help you find other users (Peers) who are downloading or sharing the same torrent. However, a Tracker can only tell you about peers that have announced the torrent to it. Even if other users are downloading the same torrent, you won't discover them through a Tracker they don't use.<br/><br/>Therefore, randomly adding more Trackers usually won't give you more available peers and will only generate additional network requests. In most cases, the Trackers included by the torrent creator are more likely to be shared by other downloaders and help you discover peers.<br/><br/>Download speed depends on the number of available peers, their upload capacity, and network conditions—not the number of Trackers.
